---
// UUIDv7: towers for a third-party benchmark (5M rows, Postgres). Static, heights to scale within each group.
// The art is built by isoart (blogs/cover-art): `isoart.py build uuid-v7/benchmark`.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import art from '../../../assets/blog/uuid-v7/benchmark.webp';
---

<div class="demo">
	<h3>Benchmark A: 5 million rows, Postgres</h3>
	<p class="try">Figures from a third-party blog post (linked in the sources), not from my machine. Heights are scaled within each group.</p>
	<Image
		src={art}
		width={1400}
		alt="Index size: bigint 107 MB, v4 285 MB, v7 118 MB. Average insert time: bigint 0.8 ms, v4 3.1 ms, v7 0.9 ms. v4 is the tallest in both groups; v7 is close to bigint."
		class="block h-auto w-full"
	/>
	<p class="note">The author notes the result assumes a steady clock and doesn't cover clock skew across several nodes.</p>
</div>
